A||N||2||johnt671||Wierd ? on Brake Master Cylinder||||5||
Z||000000||johnt671||11-28-2001||07:18 PM||||Check the brake fluid in my 84 today and noticed the rear chamber was a little low.  Added some fluid and had a hard time getting the cover back on.  Got it on and figured I should pump the brakes a few times to make sure the brakes are ok.  As I pushed down on the pedal, fluid spurted up in the rear chamber.  The car stops as good as it ever did, and the pedal is firm, but watching this happen makes me think that I don't have rear brakes.  Is this normal or do I have a problem?||||reg||5
Z||000001||PBJ||11-28-2001||09:02 PM||||Normal.  No problem.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||11-28-2001||11:45 PM||||The fact the MC tank was low is the thing to worry about. keep an eye on it and make sure it doesn't go low again anytime soon. If it does, you've got a leak.<P>The "spray" is the blow off from the QT bore in the MC. It's normal to see that. read my brake upgrade article for a short explanation of that function. (A better version was to be posted today but my PC was acting up earlier...)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
